# NOTE: this file is currently INERT, and the reason matters.
#
# Cloudflare's zone-level Browser Cache TTL (Caching > Configuration) is set to
# the 4 hour default, and it overrides origin Cache-Control for static file
# extensions. Proof: /assets/* below asks for max-age=0 and /public/* asks for
# 3600, and both come back as max-age=14400, while .html and .xml (not static
# extensions) pass through untouched at max-age=0. So the value is not coming
# from here.
#
# These rules take effect the moment Browser Cache TTL is switched to
# "Respect Existing Headers". Until then, a browser can serve a four-hour-old
# CSS file after a deploy, which is how the mobile menu fix shipped and still
# looked broken in Chrome while working in Safari on the same iPhone: Chrome on
# iOS is WebKit, so the engine was identical and only the HTTP cache differed.
#
# The ?v= token on the asset URLs in each page is the workaround that does not
# depend on the dashboard. Bump it on any deploy that changes CSS or JS, until
# the setting above is changed.
#
# Pages answers with an ETag and a 304 when nothing changed, so revalidating
# every request costs one round trip and no bytes.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Images are cosmetic when stale, so an hour rather than a round trip per view.
/public/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate
